		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=3717&amp;p=29352#p29352"><![CDATA[
Does anyone know how to configure the official firmware for true Dual Watch<br><br>I've taken my radio apart and soldered wires to the MCU/CPU to try to understand how the 2 internal transceiver chips are controlled.<br><br>With the OpenGD77, I can now set each internal transceiver to different frequencies, but I'm having problems if both channels have signals on them, but this doesn't affect the official firmware<br><br>But what the official firmware does not seem to do is be able to be receiving on a secondary channel and the switch to the primary channel if a signal is received on that channel<br><br>If both channels have no signal then it switches to whichever channel has the signal, but at the moment it does not seem to switch if its currently receiving a signal on either the primary or secondary channel<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Thu Feb 08, 2024 8:51 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
